gpty
====

gpty is the successor to two earlier projects by Sam Dotson, merged into one
cross-platform Go toolset that drives a real C tmux:

  - winmux   https://github.com/samdotson61/winmux   (native Windows tmux + wmux CLI)
  - win-pty  https://github.com/samdotson61/win-pty   (agent-pty for Windows, in Go)

Lineage and credit
-------------------
The agent-pty concept — a persistent, name-addressable PTY session abstraction
(spawn / send / snapshot / wait_for) that lets an LLM agent drive a terminal —
originates with:

    AakeshF — https://github.com/AakeshF/agent-pty

gpty re-implements that idea natively in Go over tmux, with native Windows
(MSYS2) support, PowerShell-7 panes, a tmux control-mode engine, and local
(stdio) + cloud (HTTP) MCP transports. The Go rewrite and the Windows port are
by Sam Dotson.

The upstream agent-pty project does not carry an explicit license; gpty's Go
implementation is an independent reimplementation of the design/API and claims
no rights over the upstream code. The MCP tool names (pty_spawn, pty_send, …)
and the agent-pty-<name> session prefix are preserved deliberately so gpty is a
drop-in upgrade for existing win-pty setups. If you intend to reuse the upstream
Python code, please consult the original author regarding licensing.

